# lib/sanitizers/mayo.allow — per-site PII-gate allowlist for `mayo` (mayostudios.org).
#
# One ERE per line ('#' = comment). Consumed by lib/pii-gate.sh via
# `pl onboard`'s resolve_allowlist() (it looks for lib/sanitizers/<site>.allow).
#
# Why this file exists: lib/sanitizers/mayo.sh INTENTIONALLY leaves a handful of
# published, non-PII contact points in the sanitized dump (its own PII_ALLOWLIST).
# The onboard-side gate (lib/pii-gate.sh) only ships generic defaults, so without
# this file it would flag those public contacts and fail-closed on a correctly
# sanitized dump. This mirrors mayo.sh's site-specific allowlist so the two gates
# agree. Keep it in sync with the trailing site-specific entries in
# lib/sanitizers/mayo.sh:PII_ALLOWLIST.
safety@mayostudios\.org
info@mayostudios\.org
admin@mayostudios\.org
1300 78 29 78
13 12 78
